# LRP Business Operations Package Sprint Loop

Use this loop when continuing Lending Readiness Partners **Phase 3 Business Operations Package** work (company ops — onboarding, intake, compliance, CRM, reports, sales/marketing scale, automation) without waiting for manual "merge and continue" messages.

## When triggered

- User asks to build the Business Operations Package, company ops kit, Phase 3 ops, or treat LRP as building an actual company
- User says merge and continue, execute next steps, keep moving, or similar
- Cursor Automation fires after a PR merges to `main`
- You detect `main` advanced since the last ops-package slice

## Loop steps (always in order)

1. **Sync** — `git checkout main && git pull origin main`
2. **Scope** — pick the next unchecked slice from [`docs/lrp-enterprise/04-operations/business-ops-package/00-completion-checklist.md`](../../docs/lrp-enterprise/04-operations/business-ops-package/00-completion-checklist.md)
3. **Branch** — `git checkout -b feature/lrp-ops-<short-name>` from synced `main`
4. **Implement** — claim-library-locked manuscripts under `docs/lrp-enterprise/04-operations/business-ops-package/`; update checklist; cross-link related taxonomy folders (`11-legal`, `12-compliance`, `09-crm`, `03-sales`) when content belongs there permanently
5. **Verify** — no forbidden claims; legal templates marked counsel-review; pipeline/CRM language aligned with platform enums where productized; brand + tagline + disclaimer on public-facing pieces
6. **Ship** — conventional commit, push, open PR to `main`
7. **Auto-merge** — after `gh pr create`, run:
   ```bash
   gh pr merge --auto --squash
   ```
8. **Continue** — do not stop for user input unless blocked; after merge, start step 1 again

## Slice sizing

- One section (or one major subsection for huge banks like §10 social) per PR
- Prefer full manuscripts over outlines
- Binaries under `assets/lrp/`; durable docs under `docs/lrp-enterprise/`
- Phase 4 platform features stay in Version 29.0+ product checklists — ops package specs may reference them but do not fork the product

## GitHub CLI (Windows)

`C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe`

## Blockers — stop and report

- Ambiguous legal/compliance claim that needs counsel before any template can ship
- Request for real testimonials without signed releases
- Request to fork a separate Mortgage product codebase
- Live bureau filing or guaranteed-approval marketing language
